cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  methods you use (Phillips and Sul, 2007, 2009) and, where relevant, the
  R package it ports (Sichera and Pizzuto, 2019).
type: software
title: "convergence-clubs: club convergence analysis in Python"
abstract: >-
  Phillips and Sul (2007, 2009) log t convergence test, club clustering and
  merging, validated against the R package ConvergenceClubs and the Stata
  package psecta; with sensitivity and bootstrap analysis, β- and
  σ-convergence, distribution dynamics, determinants of club membership,
  plots, maps and a one-call HTML report.
authors:
  - family-names: Banyuls
    given-names: Bernard
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/bbanyuls/club-convergence"
keywords:
  - convergence clubs
  - club convergence
  - log t test
  - Phillips and Sul
  - economic growth
  - econometrics
